# API Route Conventions

## File Location
All API routes live under `src/app/api/[name]/route.ts` following Next.js App Router conventions.

## Handler Structure
- Export one named function per HTTP method (`GET`, `POST`, `PUT`, `PATCH`, `DELETE`)
- Always return a typed `NextResponse`
- Define request/response types at the top of the file

```ts
import { NextRequest, NextResponse } from "next/server"

type ResponseBody = {
  data: string
  timestamp: string
}

export async function GET(_req: NextRequest): Promise<NextResponse<ResponseBody>> {
  return NextResponse.json({
    data: "result",
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
  })
}
```

## Error Handling
- Always return structured error responses with an appropriate HTTP status
- Never let errors bubble up unhandled

```ts
// ✅ GOOD
try {
  const result = await doSomething()
  return NextResponse.json({ data: result })
} catch (err) {
  console.error("[api/route] failed:", err)
  return NextResponse.json({ error: "Internal server error" }, { status: 500 })
}
```

## Validation
- Validate request body/params before processing — reject early with `400`
- Prefer a lightweight validation approach (zod or manual checks)

## Security
- Never expose raw error messages or stack traces to the client
- Validate and sanitize all user-provided input
